223:
(a) All persons desiring to obtain a license under this chapter for the sale of alcoholic beverages shall apply to the city upon forms to be prepared and provided by the city and shall be considered by the mayor and city council. Such application shall state:
(1) The location of the proposed business;
(2) The nature and character of the proposed business;
(3) If the business is to be operated by an individual, the name, address, and telephone number of that individual;
(4) If the business is to be operated by a partnership, the names, addresses, and telephone numbers of all general partners, the licensee, and the license representative;
(5) If the business is to be operated by a close corporation, the names, addresses, and telephone numbers of all officers, directors, stockholders, the licensee, and the license representative;
(6) If the business is to be operated by a corporation other than a close corporation, the name of the corporation, the address and telephone number of the corporate office, the name, address, and telephone number of the registered agent for service of process for the corporation, and the name, address, and telephone number of the licensee and license representative;
(7) If the business is to be operated by a limited liability company ("LLC"), the name of the managing partner or partners, the address and telephone number of the principal place of business of the LLC, the name, address, and telephone number of the registered agent for service of process for the LLC, and the name, address, and telephone number of the licensee or license representative;
(8) Individuals who shall be listed on an application pursuant to subsections (a)(3) through (a)(7) above shall be required to undergo a background investigation, which may include a check through Georgia Crime Information Center and/or National Crime Information Center of such person, and shall fully comply with the process of conducting said investigation and shall supply information necessary to conduct said investigation as requested on the application; and
(9) Such other appropriate information as may be required by the governing body.
(b) The truth of the contents of an application for a license shall be sworn to by the licensee and the license representative.
(c) The licensee shall also file with the city a completed State of Georgia Department of Revenue Alcohol Tax and Control Unit form ATT-17, which has been filed with the state, if applicable.
(d) The application, when filed with the city, shall be accompanied by a processing fee of $500.00, plus $35.00 per individual that is subject to a background check pursuant to this section or section 6-101 or as otherwise required under this chapter. The processing fee and background check fee is payable by certified check or cash and is separate from and shall not be credited to the license fee. Said processing fee will not be refunded if the requested license is not granted.
(Ord. No. 2015-006, § 1(Exh. A), 8-10-2015)
